msgid "Glitch Analysis: Q-Transform and Omega-Scan"
msgstr "グリッチ詳細解析：Q-変換と Omega スキャン"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_glitch_analysis.ipynb:10004
#: e3cfd5acdfe24151aaf4d02ed7ba791a
msgid ""
"**Glitches** are short-duration, non-Gaussian noise transients that "
"contaminate gravitational-wave data.  The **Q-transform** (or Omega scan) is"
" the standard time-frequency representation used to characterise and "
"classify glitches at all major detector sites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_glitch_analysis.ipynb:10009
#: f85449b779f6416e8e092446fed264b5
msgid ""
"The Q-transform tiles the time-frequency plane with constant-Q (constant "
"bandwidth-to-frequency ratio) windows and measures the normalised energy in "
"each tile.  A glitch appears as a cluster of tiles with anomalously high "
"SNR."
msgstr ""

